Article 1 (Purpose)
The purpose of this Decree is to prescribe matters delegated by the Act on Fostering and Supporting Agricultural and Fisheries Business Entities and matters necessary for its enforcement.

Article 2 (Agricultural Business Information and Fisheries Business Information Subject to Registration)
(1) The term “matters prescribed by Presidential Decree” in Article 4 (1) 1 and 2 of the Act on Fostering and Supporting Agricultural and Fisheries Business Entities (hereinafter referred to as the “Act”) means, respectively, the information specified in the following subparagraphs: <Amended on September 9, 2011; March 23, 2013; April 30, 2014; September 19, 2017; August 26, 2020>
1. Information related to agricultural business: Information specified in attached Table 1;
2. Information related to fisheries business: Names and addresses of fishers; corporate names of fisheries corporations and names and addresses of their representatives; status of licenses, permits, and reports for fishing and aquaculture; areas of fishing facilities and aquaculture facilities; sizes of fishing vessels; forms of business operation; production quantities by fish species and product; and other information prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Oceans and Fisheries as necessary for fostering and supporting agricultural business entities.
(2) The phrase “where important matters prescribed by Presidential Decree have changed” in the latter part of Article 4 (1) of the Act, excluding its subparagraphs, means any of the following cases: <Amended on September 9, 2011; March 23, 2013; April 30, 2014; December 24, 2018; August 26, 2020>
1. Where information under 1 (a), 3 (a), 4 (a), 6 (a), or 7 (a) of attached Table 1, or other information prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs, has changed;
2. Where information under 4 (b), 6 (c), or 7 (b) of attached Table 1, or other information prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs, has changed beyond the range determined and publicly notified by the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs;
3. Where, among the information under paragraph (1) 2, the names and addresses of fishers, the corporate names of fisheries corporations and the names and addresses of their representatives, the status of licenses, permits, and reports for fishing and aquaculture, or the sizes of fishing vessels have changed;
4. Where, among the information under paragraph (1) 2, the areas of fishing facilities and aquaculture facilities or production quantities by fish species and product have changed beyond the range determined and publicly notified by the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries.

Article 2-2 (Registration Criteria for Agricultural and Fisheries Business Information)
(1) The registration criteria for agricultural business information under Article 4 (1) 1 of the Act shall be as specified in the following categories:
1. Farmers: Meet all of the following requirements:
(a) Have a lawful entitlement to means of production, such as farmland, livestock sheds, forest land, and horticultural facilities;
(b) Have a record of sales of agricultural products directly produced or a record of agricultural business operations, such as the use of agricultural materials;
2. Agricultural corporations: Meet all of the following requirements:
(a) Have a lawful entitlement to means of production, such as farmland, livestock sheds, forest land, and horticultural facilities (applicable only where there are means of production);
(b) Have a record of business operations and activities relating to agricultural management.
(2) The registration criteria for fisheries business information under Article 4 (1) 2 of the Act shall be as specified in the following categories:
1. Fishers: Meet all of the following requirements:
(a) Be lawfully qualified to engage in fishing or aquaculture under the relevant statutes and regulations;
(b) Have a record of sales of fishery products directly produced, or a record of engaging in fishing or aquaculture for at least a specified period determined by the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries;
2. Fisheries corporations: Have a record of business operations and activities relating to the management of fishing or aquaculture businesses.
(3) The details and application of the registration criteria under paragraphs (1) and (2) shall be determined and publicly notified by the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs or the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries.

Article 3 (Methods of Providing Data)
Where the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs or the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries requests the heads of relevant central administrative agencies, etc. to submit relevant data pursuant to Article 5 (1) of the Act, the heads of relevant central administrative agencies, etc. may provide the data electronically, including through links between the information systems of institutions. <Amended on March 23, 2013>

Article 4 (Investigation and Verification of Registered Information)
When intending to conduct an investigation and verification under Article 6-2 (1) 6 of the Act, the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs or the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries shall verify the following information submitted pursuant to Article 5 (1) of the Act and, where necessary, have relevant public officials conduct an on-site investigation under paragraph (2) of that Article:
1. Information concerning reports on the establishment, changes, or dissolution of agricultural corporations or fisheries corporations under Articles 16 (3) and 19 (5) of the Act;
2. Information concerning the history of livestock managed through the traceability management system under Article 27 (2) of the Act on Livestock and Livestock Products Traceability;
3. Information concerning reports on insect production businesses under Article 12 of the Act on Fostering and Supporting the Insect Industry;
4. Information concerning reports on ornamental fish aquaculture businesses under Article 12 of the Act on Fostering and Supporting the Ornamental Fish Industry;
5. Information registered in land registers and forest land registers under Article 71 of the Act on the Establishment and Management of Spatial Data, Etc.;
6. Information concerning fishing licenses, permits, or reports under Article 6, 9, or 11 of the Inland Water Fisheries Act;
7. Information entered in farmland registers under Article 49 of the Farmland Act;
8. Information concerning permits for salt manufacturing businesses under Article 23 (1) 2 or 3 of the Salt Industry Promotion Act (including cases of operating a salt manufacturing business after entering into a lease agreement or loan-for-use agreement for a salt pan covered by a permit);
9. Information concerning fishing licenses, permits, or reports under Article 7, 40, or 48 of the Fisheries Act;
10. Information concerning permits for fishery seed production businesses under Article 21 of the Fishery Seed Industry Promotion Act;
11. Information concerning registration of beekeeping farms under Article 13 of the Act on Fostering and Supporting the Beekeeping Industry;
12. Information concerning aquaculture licenses or permits under Article 10 or 43 of the Aquaculture Industry Development Act;
13. Information concerning permits and reports for distant water fishing under Article 6 of the Distant Water Fisheries Development Act;
14. Computerized resident registration information under Article 30 of the Resident Registration Act;
15. Information concerning surveys of the actual conditions of grassland management under Article 24 of the Grassland Act;
16. Information concerning permits for breeding stock businesses, hatchery businesses, or livestock raising businesses under Article 22 (1) of the Livestock Industry Act, or registration of livestock raising businesses under paragraph (3) of that Article;
17. Information concerning farmland under Article 19, 22, or 24-4 of the Korea Rural Community Corporation and Farmland Management Fund Act.

Article 5 (Reports on Establishment, Etc. of Farming Association Corporations and Fisheries Association Corporations)
(1) A person intending to file a report on the establishment, a change, or dissolution of a farming association corporation under Article 16 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as a “farming association corporation”) or a fisheries association corporation under paragraph (2) of that Article (hereinafter referred to as a “fisheries association corporation”) pursuant to paragraph (3) of that Article shall submit a report, accompanied by documents prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs or Ordinance of the Ministry of Oceans and Fisheries, to the head of a Si/Gun/Gu having jurisdiction over the location of its principal office (in the case of the head of a Si, referring to the Special Self-Governing Province Governor for a Special Self-Governing Province and the Special Self-Governing City Mayor for a Special Self-Governing City; hereinafter the same shall apply; in the case of the head of a Gu, referring to the head of an autonomous Gu; hereinafter the same shall apply).
(2) The term “important matters prescribed by Presidential Decree” in the latter part of Article 16 (3) of the Act means the following matters:
1. Name;
2. Purpose;
3. Business;
4. Location of offices;
5. Names of the members who are to represent farming association corporations and fisheries association corporations (hereinafter referred to as “association corporations”) and of their officers (limited to association corporations that have directors and auditors);
6. Total number of contribution units and total amount of paid-in capital contributions;
7. Matters concerning the methods of payment and calculation of capital contributions and the maximum amount that any one member may contribute;
8. Grounds for dissolution (applicable only where grounds for dissolution have been specified).
(3) The head of a Si/Gun/Gu may return a report submitted pursuant to paragraph (1) where any of the following subparagraphs applies:
1. Where the procedures for the establishment, change, or dissolution of an association corporation violate statutes or regulations;
2. Where the contents of the articles of incorporation or report violate statutes or regulations;
3. Where the report has not been supplemented within the specified period after a request for supplementation under paragraph (4) has been received.
(4) Where supplementation of the contents of a report submitted pursuant to paragraph (1) is necessary, the head of a Si/Gun/Gu may specify a period of no more than 20 days and request the person filing the report to supplement it.

Article 6 Deleted. <September 19, 2017>

Article 7 Deleted. <September 19, 2017>

Article 8 Deleted. <August 6, 2014>

