Article 10 (Capital Contributions to Association Corporations)
(1) Members of a farming association corporation may make capital contributions in farmland, cash, or other contributions in kind, as prescribed by the articles of incorporation.
(2) Members of a fisheries association corporation may make capital contributions in fishing grounds, cash, or other contributions in kind, as prescribed by the articles of incorporation.

Article 11 Deleted. <May 9, 2022>

Article 12 (Matters to Be Stated in Articles of Incorporation)
(1) The articles of incorporation of an association corporation shall include the following matters:
1. Name;
2. Purpose;
3. Business;
4. Location of offices;
5. Matters concerning the eligibility of members (including associate members; hereinafter the same shall apply in this paragraph);
6. Matters concerning the admission, withdrawal, and expulsion of members;
7. Matters concerning the calculation of equity interests upon the withdrawal or expulsion of members;
8. Matters concerning the methods of payment and calculation of capital contributions and the maximum amount that any one member may contribute;
9. Matters concerning the treatment of profits and losses;
10. Matters concerning the ratio of reserves and the methods of accumulating them;
11. Matters concerning the fiscal year and accounting;
12. Matters concerning the general meeting or other decision-making bodies, and the number, election, and dismissal of officers;
13. Where grounds for dissolution have been specified, matters concerning those grounds.
(2) For the efficient establishment of association corporations, the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs or the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries may establish model articles of incorporation for association corporations and recommend their use as the standard for drafting articles of incorporation. <Amended on March 23, 2013>

Article 13 (Dissolution of Association Corporations)
An association corporation shall be dissolved where any of the following subparagraphs applies: <Amended on July 6, 2015; August 26, 2020>
1. Where the general meeting adopts a resolution for dissolution;
2. Where the association corporation is merged;
3. Where the association corporation becomes bankrupt;
4. Where a court orders its dissolution under Article 176 of the Commercial Act, which applies mutatis mutandis pursuant to Article 20-3 (1) of the Act;
5. Where the number of members fails to reach at least 5 within 1 year after falling below 5 (excluding a fisheries association corporation that has obtained a cooperative aquaculture license);
6. Where any other ground for dissolution specified in the articles of incorporation occurs.

Article 13-2 (Registration of Incorporation of Association Corporations)
(1) Registration of incorporation of an association corporation under Article 16-3 (1) of the Act shall be applied for by the member who is to represent the association corporation. <Amended on May 9, 2022>
(2) The matters to be registered for incorporation of an association corporation under paragraph (1) shall be as follows: <Amended on August 6, 2014>
1. Matters under Article 12 (1) 1 through 4, 8, and 13;
2. Addresses and names of the members who are to represent the association corporation and of its officers (limited to association corporations that have directors and auditors);
3. Where it has been stipulated that at least 2 members are to represent the association corporation jointly, that provision;
4. Total number of contribution units and total amount of paid-in capital contributions.
(3) An application for registration of incorporation under paragraph (1) shall be accompanied by the following documents: <Amended on August 6, 2014; December 22, 2015; May 9, 2022>
1. Minutes of the inaugural general meeting;
2. Articles of incorporation;
3. A document stating the details of assets contributed;
4. A document proving that the member is to represent the association corporation;
5. In the case of a farming association corporation, documents verifying that at least 5 members are farmers or producer organizations under subparagraph 4 of Article 3 of the Framework Act on Agriculture, Rural Community and Food Industry (hereinafter referred to as “agricultural producer organizations”);
6. In the case of a fisheries association corporation, documents verifying that at least 5 members are fishers or producer organizations under subparagraph 5 of Article 3 of the Framework Act on Fisheries and Fishing Villages Development (hereinafter referred to as “fisheries producer organizations”);
7. A certificate confirming the filing of a report on establishment under Article 16-2 (1) of the Act.

Article 13-3 (Registration of Changes to Association Corporations)
(1) Registration of changes under Article 16-3 (2) of the Act shall be applied for by the member representing the association corporation. <Amended on May 9, 2022>
(2) The term “important matters prescribed by Presidential Decree” in Article 16-3 (2) of the Act means the matters under the subparagraphs of Article 5 (2). <Added on May 9, 2022>
(3) To register changes pursuant to Article 16-3 (2) of the Act, an application for registration of changes shall be submitted with the following documents attached: Provided, That the documents under subparagraphs 2 and 3 shall be attached only where changes resulting from a merger or division are being registered: <Amended on May 9, 2022>
1. Documents proving changes to registered matters;
2. Documents proving that public notice was given pursuant to Article 18-2 (5) of the Act;
3. Documents proving that debts were repaid or collateral was provided to creditors who filed objections pursuant to Article 18-2 (6) of the Act;
4. A certificate confirming the filing of a report on changes under Article 16-2 (1) of the Act.

Article 13-4 (Registration of Dissolution of Association Corporations)
(1) Registration of dissolution under Article 16-3 (2) of the Act shall be applied for by the liquidator.
(2) An application for registration of dissolution under paragraph (1) shall be accompanied by the following documents:
1. Documents proving the grounds for dissolution;
2. A certificate confirming the filing of a report on dissolution under Article 16-2 (1) of the Act.

Article 14 (Qualifications for Associate Membership)
(1) Persons eligible to join a farming association corporation as associate members pursuant to Article 17(2) of the Act shall be as follows: <Amended on December 9, 2014>
1. Persons supplying production materials or providing production technology to the farming association corporation;
2. Persons leasing farmland to the farming association corporation or entrusting the management of farmland to it;
3. Persons purchasing, distributing, processing, or exporting agricultural products produced by the farming association corporation;
4. Other persons who are not farmers and who make capital contributions to the farming association corporation to participate in its business.
(2) Persons eligible to join a fisheries association corporation as associate members pursuant to Article 17(6) of the Act shall be as follows: <Amended on July 6, 2015>
1. Persons supplying production materials or providing production technology and capital to the fisheries association corporation;
2. Bulk end users, distributors, and processors of fishery products produced by the fisheries association corporation.

Article 15 (Membership of Farming Association Corporations in Producer Organizations)
The agricultural producer organizations that a farming association corporation may join as a member or associate member pursuant to Article 17(4) of the Act shall be agricultural cooperatives, forestry cooperatives, and leaf tobacco producers' cooperatives. <Amended on July 6, 2015>

Article 16 (Qualifications of Members of Fisheries Association Corporations Eligible to Obtain Cooperative Aquaculture Business Licenses and Related Matters)
Members of a fisheries association corporation eligible to obtain a cooperative aquaculture business license pursuant to Article 11(2) of the Aquaculture Industry Development Act shall be persons with any of the following qualifications: <Amended on August 26, 2020>
1. A member of a fishing village association whose district covers the water area for which the cooperative aquaculture business license is sought;
2. A member of a district fisheries cooperative whose address is within the district of the fishing village association under subparagraph 1.

Article 17 (Forms of Establishment of Agricultural Companies and Fisheries Companies)
(1) Farmers and agricultural producer organizations may establish an agricultural company in any of the following forms pursuant to Article 19(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as an "agricultural company"): <Amended on June 4, 2019; May 9, 2022>
1. An unlimited partnership company;
2. A limited partnership company;
2-2. A limited liability company;
3. A stock company;
4. A limited company.
(2) Fishers and fisheries producer organizations may establish a fisheries company in any of the following forms pursuant to Article 19(3) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as a "fisheries company"): <Amended on June 4, 2019; May 9, 2022>
1. An unlimited partnership company;
2. A limited partnership company;
2-2. A limited liability company;
3. A stock company;
4. A limited company.
(3) Deleted. <May 9, 2022>
(4) Deleted. <May 9, 2022>

Article 18 (Limits on Capital Contributions by Persons Other Than Farmers, Fishers, or Producer Organizations)
(1) The limits on capital contributions to agricultural companies by persons other than farmers or agricultural producer organizations pursuant to Article 19(2) of the Act shall be as follows:
1. Where the total capital contributions to an agricultural company are 8 billion won or less: 90 percent of the total capital contributions;
2. Where the total capital contributions to an agricultural company exceed 8 billion won: The amount remaining after deducting 800 million won from the total capital contributions.
(2) The limits on capital contributions to fisheries companies by persons other than fishers or fisheries producer organizations pursuant to Article 19(4) of the Act shall be as follows:
1. Where the total capital contributions to a fisheries company are 8 billion won or less: 90 percent of the total capital contributions;
2. Where the total capital contributions to a fisheries company exceed 8 billion won: The amount remaining after deducting 800 million won from the total capital contributions.

Article 19 (Reporting the Establishment of Agricultural Companies and Fisheries Companies and Related Matters)
(1) A person intending to report the establishment of, changes to, or dissolution of an agricultural company or fisheries company pursuant to Article 19(5) of the Act shall submit a report, accompanied by documents prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs or Ordinance of the Ministry of Oceans and Fisheries, to the head of the Si/Gun/Gu having jurisdiction over the location of its principal office.
(2) "Important matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the latter part of Article 19(5) of the Act means the following matters:
1. Name;
2. Purpose;
3. Business activities;
4. Location of the office;
5. Names of officers;
6. Total number of units of capital contributions, total number of shares, and total amount of paid-in capital contributions;
7. Matters concerning the methods of payment and calculation of capital contributions and the maximum amount that any one member or shareholder may contribute;
8. Grounds for dissolution (applicable only where grounds for dissolution have been specified).
(3) The head of a Si/Gun/Gu may return a report submitted pursuant to paragraph (1) in any of the following cases:
1. Where the procedures for establishment, alteration, or dissolution of an agricultural company or fisheries company (hereinafter referred to as a "company") violate statutes or regulations;
2. Where the contents of the articles of incorporation or the report violate statutes or regulations;
3. Where the reporting person fails to supplement the report within the specified period after receiving a request to do so under paragraph (4).
(4) Where the contents of a report submitted pursuant to paragraph (1) require supplementation, the head of a Si/Gun/Gu may set a period of not more than 20 days and request that the reporting person supplement the report within that period.

Article 20 (Preparation of Model Articles of Incorporation)
To facilitate the efficient establishment of agricultural companies or fisheries companies, the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs or the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries may prescribe model articles of incorporation for agricultural companies or fisheries companies and recommend their use as a standard for preparing articles of incorporation. <Amended on March 23, 2013>

Article 20-2 (Registration of Establishment of Companies)
When applying for registration of establishment of a company pursuant to Article 19-3(1) of the Act, the following documents shall accompany the application for registration of establishment:
1. Documents verifying that the persons intending to establish the company pursuant to Article 17(1) or (2) are farmers, agricultural producer organizations, fishers, or fisheries producer organizations;
2. Documents for the applicable category below that enable verification of compliance with the limits on capital contributions under Article 18(1) or (2):
(a) Where the company is established in the form of a stock company: Documents indicating each share subscriber's name, address, number of shares subscribed for, and whether the subscriber is a farmer, agricultural producer organization, fisher, or fisheries producer organization, and documents verifying that the relevant share subscriber is a farmer, agricultural producer organization, fisher, or fisheries producer organization;
(b) Where the company is established in a form other than a stock company: A list of members who are farmers, agricultural producer organizations, fishers, or fisheries producer organizations, and documents verifying that the relevant members are farmers, agricultural producer organizations, fishers, or fisheries producer organizations;
3. A certificate confirming the establishment report under Article 19-2(1) of the Act.

Article 20-3 (Registration of Changes to Companies)
(1) "Important matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 19-3(2) of the Act means the matters in each subparagraph of Article 19(2).
(2) When applying for registration of changes to a company pursuant to Article 19-3(2) of the Act, the following documents shall accompany the application for registration of changes:
1. Documents proving the changes to registered matters;
2. A certificate confirming the report of changes under Article 19-2(1) of the Act.

Article 20-4 (Registration of Dissolution of Companies)
When applying for registration of dissolution of a company pursuant to Article 19-3(2) of the Act, the following documents shall accompany the application for registration of dissolution:
1. Documents proving the grounds for dissolution;
2. A certificate confirming the dissolution report under Article 19-2(1) of the Act.

Article 20-5 (Scope of Business Activities of Agricultural Corporations and Fisheries Corporations)
(1) "Business activities prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as agricultural operations and the joint shipment, distribution, or processing of agricultural products" in Article 19-4(1) of the Act means the following business activities:
1. Agricultural operations;
2. Shipment, distribution, processing, sale, and export of agricultural products;
3. Performance of agricultural work on behalf of others;
4. Tourism and recreation businesses in agricultural and fishing villages;
5. Rural convergence industry under the Act on Fostering and Supporting Rural Convergence Industry (applicable only where conducted as a rural convergence industry business operator);
6. The following incidental business activities:
(a) Production and supply of materials necessary for farming;
(b) Production of seeds and cultivation of spawn necessary for farming;
(c) Purchase and stockpiling of agricultural products;
(d) Rental, repair, and storage of agricultural machinery or other equipment;
(e) Acceptance of entrustment of, and management of, small-scale irrigation facilities;
(f) Establishment and operation of facilities for joint use in connection with agriculture.
(2) "Business activities prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as fisheries operations and the joint shipment, distribution, or processing of fishery products" in Article 19-4(2) of the Act means the following business activities: <Amended on January 10, 2023>
1. Operation of fishing and aquaculture businesses;
2. Shipment, distribution, processing, sale, and export of fishery products;
3. Performance of fishing work on behalf of others;
4. Tourism and recreation businesses in agricultural and fishing villages;
5. Fishing ground businesses under the Fishing Management and Promotion Act;
6. Operation of recreational fishing grounds under Article 62(1) of the Fisheries Act (applicable only to fisheries association corporations);
7. Fishing village and fishery harbor regeneration projects under the Fishing Villages and Fishery Harbors Act (applicable only to fisheries association corporations);
8. The following incidental business activities:
(a) Production and supply of materials necessary for fishing operations;
(b) Production of fishery seeds necessary for fishing operations;
(c) Purchase and stockpiling of fishery products;
(d) Rental, repair, and storage of fisheries equipment and other such equipment;
(e) Establishment and operation of facilities for joint use in connection with fisheries.

Article 20-6 (Information Related to Fact-Finding Surveys)
"Information prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as computerized corporate registration information, taxation information, and information from real estate transaction reports" in Article 20-2(6) of the Act means the following information concerning agricultural corporations and fisheries corporations:
1. Computerized registration information under the Commercial Registration Act;
2. Business registration numbers and types of business, among business registration information under the Value-Added Tax Act;
3. Sales revenue under the Corporate Tax Act and shareholder information shown in the statement of changes in stocks, etc. under that Act;
4. Information from reports of real estate transactions under the Act on Report on Real Estate Transactions, Etc.

Article 20-7 (Period for Correction)
The head of a Si/Gun/Gu may order that matters under each subparagraph of Article 20-2(8) of the Act be corrected within 6 months: Provided, That, where there are unavoidable grounds, the period may be extended only once for up to 3 months. <Amended on September 19, 2017; May 9, 2022>

Article 20-8 (Detailed Criteria for Imposing Penalty Surcharges and Related Matters)
(1) The detailed criteria for imposing penalty surcharges under Article 20-4(1) of the Act shall be as specified in Annex 1-2.
(2) Where the head of a Si/Gun/Gu intends to impose a penalty surcharge pursuant to Article 20-4(1) of the Act, the head shall give written notice requiring payment, specifying the type of violation and the amount of the penalty surcharge.
(3) A person receiving a notice under paragraph (2) shall pay the penalty surcharge to a collecting institution designated by the head of the Si/Gun/Gu within 60 days from the date of receipt of the notice. <Amended on December 12, 2023>
(4) A collecting institution receiving payment of a penalty surcharge pursuant to paragraph (3) shall issue a receipt to the payer.
(5) Upon collecting a penalty surcharge pursuant to paragraph (3), the collecting institution shall notify the head of the Si/Gun/Gu of that fact without delay.

Article 20-9 (Establishment and Operation of the Comprehensive Information System)
(1) "Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 20-5(2)7 of the Act means matters concerning the receipt of subsidies among the information registered as agricultural and fisheries business information pursuant to Article 4(1) of the Act. <Amended on February 6, 2024>
(2) Details necessary for the establishment and operation of the comprehensive information management system, other than those provided for in paragraph (1), shall be determined by the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs or the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries.

Article 20-10 (Scope of Information Subject to Entry or Submission)
The scope of information subject to entry in or submission to the integrated agricultural education information system or integrated fisheries education information system under Article 25(2) of the Act shall be as follows: <Amended on May 9, 2022>
1. The name of the educational course, persons to be educated, purpose and necessity of the education, educational contents, place of education, and timing of education;
2. The names, dates of birth, sex, addresses, contact details, and fields of instruction of instructors participating in the education;
3. The names, dates of birth, sex, addresses, and contact details of persons participating in the education, and the crops they cultivate;
4. Agricultural and fisheries business information registered pursuant to Article 4(1) of the Act;
5. Information concerning support for management and technical education, specialized consulting, and other services under Article 22(1) of the Act;
6. Information concerning professional agricultural or fisheries business managers under Article 22(2) of the Act;
7. Other information relevant and necessary for the education of agricultural and fisheries business entities.

Article 21 (Requirements for Designation of Specialized Institutions for Agricultural and Fisheries Human Resources Development and Related Matters)
(1) A person eligible for designation as a specialized institution for agricultural and fisheries human resources development pursuant to Article 27(1) of the Act shall meet all of the following requirements: <Amended on January 5, 2021>
1. The person shall have a system, including an organization and personnel, capable of performing the role under Article 27(1) of the Act;
2. The person shall have expertise in education for farmers and fishers.
(2) A person intending to be designated as a specialized institution for agricultural and fisheries human resources development pursuant to Article 27(1) of the Act shall meet the requirements for designation under paragraph (1) and submit an operational plan concerning the implementation, research, evaluation, and project management of education, specialized consulting, and other services for agricultural and fisheries business entities to the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs or the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries. <Amended on March 23, 2013>

Article 21-2 (Duties of Institutions Dedicated to Evaluation and Performance Management of Projects Supporting Agricultural and Fisheries Business Entities and Related Matters)
(1) The Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs or the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries may have an institution dedicated to evaluation and performance management of projects supporting agricultural and fisheries business entities under Article 27-2(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as a "dedicated institution") perform the following duties:
1. Accumulation and analysis of data necessary for the planning, management, evaluation, and other aspects of projects supporting agricultural and fisheries business entities;
2. Inspection of the status of implementation of projects supporting agricultural and fisheries business entities;
3. Evaluation of the performance of projects supporting agricultural and fisheries business entities;
4. Matters necessary for reorganizing the project implementation system, improving institutional arrangements, and improving regulations to enhance the efficiency of projects supporting agricultural and fisheries business entities;
5. Other matters determined by the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs or the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries.
(2) The requirements for designation of dedicated institutions shall be as specified in Annex 2.
(3) A person intending to be designated as a dedicated institution shall submit an application for designation as a dedicated institution in the form prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs or Ordinance of the Ministry of Oceans and Fisheries, accompanied by the following documents, to the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs or the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries:
1. Articles of incorporation or equivalent rules concerning business operations;
2. A plan for performing the duties in each subparagraph of paragraph (1);
3. Details of the specialized personnel and facilities possessed;
4. A record of performance of relevant duties.
(4) Where the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs or the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries designates a dedicated institution or revokes its designation, the Minister shall post that fact on the website of the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs or the Ministry of Oceans and Fisheries.

Article 21-3 (Requirements for Designation of Joint Agricultural Business Entities)
(1) The area under joint management and the number of participating agricultural business entities required of a corporation or organization seeking designation as a joint agricultural business entity pursuant to Article 27-3 (2) 3 of the Act shall be as follows, respectively:
1. Area under joint management: At least 50 hectares;
2. Number of participating agricultural business entities: At least 25 farmers.
(2) Notwithstanding paragraph (1), the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs may prescribe and publicly notify different requirements from those under the subparagraphs of paragraph (1), according to the characteristics of the agricultural product items that a joint agricultural business entity intends to produce and the geographical conditions of that entity.

Article 21-4 (Education for Designation as Joint Agricultural Business Entities)
(1) Education necessary for operating a joint agricultural business entity under Article 27-3 (2) 4 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "education for joint agricultural business entities" in this Article) means either of the following:
1. Education on management and technology for joint agricultural business entities or on organizing and scaling up joint agricultural business entities, provided by the State or a local government and prescribed by the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs;
2. Education concerning the organization and scaling up of joint agricultural business entities provided by the Korea Agency of Education, Promotion and Information Service in Food, Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries under Article 11-2 of the Framework Act on Agriculture, Rural Community and Food Industry.
(2) The representative of a corporation or the head of an organization seeking designation as a joint agricultural business entity shall receive education for joint agricultural business entities: Provided, That where the representative of the corporation or the head of the organization required to receive such education is not a farmer, another farmer managing the joint agricultural business entity may receive the education in that person's place.
(3) Education for joint agricultural business entities shall be at least eight hours in duration.

Article 21-5 (Procedures for Designation of Joint Agricultural Business Entities)
(1) A corporation or organization seeking designation as a joint agricultural business entity pursuant to Article 27-3 (1) of the Act shall, pursuant to paragraph (3) of that Article, submit to the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs an application prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs, accompanied by the following materials:
1. Materials that can prove that the requirements under the subparagraphs of Article 27-3 (2) of the Act have been satisfied;
2. A letter of recommendation from the head of a Si/Gun/Gu under Article 27-3 (3) of the Act.
(2) Where the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs designates a joint agricultural business entity pursuant to Article 27-3 (4) of the Act, the Minister shall issue a certificate of designation prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs.

Article 21-6 (Agricultural Business Information of Joint Agricultural Business Entities and Agricultural Business Information Subject to Registration of Changes)
(1) Agricultural business information of joint agricultural business entities under the former part of Article 27-4 (1) of the Act shall be as specified in Annex 2-2.
(2) "Important matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the latter part of Article 27-4 (1) of the Act means the following:
1. The name of the joint agricultural business entity;
2. The representative of the joint agricultural business entity;
3. Farmers participating in the joint agricultural business entity;
4. The location of the principal office of the joint agricultural business entity;
5. Contact information of the joint agricultural business entity;
6. The operating plan of the joint agricultural business entity under Article 27-3 (2) 1 of the Act;
7. Internal rules on joint management under Article 27-3 (2) 2 of the Act;
8. The area of farmland under joint management by the joint agricultural business entity.

Article 22 (Delegation and Entrustment of Authority)
(1) Pursuant to Article 29 (1) of the Act, the Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs or the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries shall delegate the following authority to the head of the National Agricultural Products Quality Management Service or the head of a Regional Office of Oceans and Fisheries: Provided, That authority concerning information subject to registration relating to forest land in Annex 1, from among the following authority, shall be delegated to the Minister of the Korea Forest Service: <Amended on September 19, 2017; December 24, 2018; February 6, 2024>
